    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d787">

                <pb facs="1013" n="917" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg917"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Mr. Hay.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-10-04"><hi rendition="#italic">October 4,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2.]</seg></opener>
                <p>The opinions of Admiral Dewey, in the possession of the commission, seem to favor
                    retention of Luzon alone, but appear to have been given in answer to question as
                    to which island in Philippine Islands the United States should retain. If this
                    assumption is correct will you, if it is deemed advisable, ascertain by
                    telegraph through proper channel, and telegraph us whether Admiral has formed an
                    opinion and, if so, what it is on the question whether it would be better for
                    United States to retain Luzon and perhaps one or two small adjacent islands or
                    the whole group?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Day.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
